#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:2
msgid "Direct upload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:4
msgid ""
"Direct upload lets you build your documentation anywhere, for example in "
"GitHub Actions or in any other continuous integration service, and upload "
"the resulting files to Read the Docs for hosting. This guide shows how to "
"build your documentation in your own pipeline and upload it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:9
msgid ""
"Documentation uploaded this way keeps all the hosting features you already "
"know: :doc:`versions </versions>`, :doc:`pull request previews </pull-"
"requests>`, :doc:`server side search </server-side-search/index>`, :doc:"
"`Addons </addons>`, :doc:`custom domains </custom-domains>` and :doc:"
"`downloadable formats </offline-formats>`, among others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:15
msgid "Direct upload is useful when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:17
msgid ""
"Your documentation tool is not supported by the Read the Docs build process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:18
msgid ""
"Your build needs tools, secrets or resources that are only available in your "
"own environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:19
msgid ""
"You already build the documentation in your continuous integration pipeline "
"and want to reuse the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Direct upload is currently a beta testing feature.** It has to be enabled "
"on your project, and we ask that you give us feedback on it. :doc:`Contact "
"support </support>` to enable it on your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:27
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:29
msgid ""
"A project on Read the Docs, with direct upload enabled by our support team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:30
msgid ""
"An :ref:`API token <api/v3:Token>` belonging to a user with admin access to "
"the project. Store it as a secret in your continuous integration service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:35
msgid ""
"We are working on project-scoped tokens, which give access to a single "
"project instead of everything the user can access. They will be released "
"soon, and we recommend switching to them once available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:40
msgid "Uploading from GitHub Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:42
msgid ""
"Use the `upload action <https://github.com/readthedocs/upload-action>`__ "
"after the step that builds your documentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:45
msgid ".github/workflows/docs.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:45
msgid ""
"name: Docs\n"
"\n"
"on:\n"
"  push:\n"
"    branches: [main]\n"
"    tags: [\"v*\"]\n"
"  pull_request:\n"
"\n"
"jobs:\n"
"  docs:\n"
"    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n"
"    # Pull requests from forks don't have access to secrets.\n"
"    # Do not use ``pull_request_target`` to work around this because it "
"would run\n"
"    # the pull request's code with access to your token.\n"
"    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository\n"
"    steps:\n"
"      - uses: actions/checkout@v5\n"
"\n"
"      # Build your documentation using the tool you are already using\n"
"      #\n"
"      # Building with Sphinx as example:\n"
"      #\n"
"      # - uses: actions/setup-python@v6\n"
"      #   with:\n"
"      #     python-version: \"3.14\"\n"
"      # - run: pip install -r docs/requirements.txt\n"
"      # - run: sphinx-build -b html docs/ _build/html\n"
"\n"
"      - uses: readthedocs/upload-action@v1\n"
"        with:\n"
"          token: ${{ secrets.READTHEDOCS_TOKEN }}\n"
"          project-slug: <your-project-slug>\n"
"          html: _build/html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:82
msgid ""
"The workflow reads the API token from a secret named ``READTHEDOCS_TOKEN``. "
"Add it to your repository under :menuselection:`Settings --> Secrets and "
"variables --> Actions`, or follow `GitHub's guide on using secrets <https://"
"docs.github.com/en/actions/security-for-github-actions/security-guides/using-"
"secrets-in-github-actions>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:86
msgid ""
"The upload action detects the branch, tag or pull request from the workflow "
"event, so a push to ``main`` updates the ``main`` version, a new tag creates "
"a new version, and a pull request creates a :doc:`pull request preview </"
"pull-requests>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:93
msgid "Uploading from any other environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:95
msgid ""
"The upload action is a thin wrapper around the `readthedocs-upload <https://"
"pypi.org/project/readthedocs-upload/>`__ package, a command line client that "
"you can run from any continuous integration service or from your own "
"computer. It requires Python 3.10 or newer and reads the token from the "
"``READTHEDOCS_TOKEN`` environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:99
msgid ""
"$ export READTHEDOCS_TOKEN=<token>\n"
"$ uvx --from readthedocs-upload readthedocs upload --project-slug <your-"
"project-slug> --html _build/html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:104
msgid ""
"You can also install it with ``pip install readthedocs-upload``, which makes "
"the ``readthedocs`` command available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:107
msgid ""
"Outside GitHub Actions, the client infers the version from the local Git "
"checkout. On other continuous integration services, pass the version "
"explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:110
msgid ""
"$ readthedocs upload \\\n"
"    --project-slug <your-project-slug> \\\n"
"    --html _build/html \\\n"
"    --version-name <branch, tag or pull request number> \\\n"
"    --version-type <branch, tag or external> \\\n"
"    --commit <full commit hash>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:119
msgid "Run ``readthedocs upload --help`` to see all the options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:122
msgid "Uploading offline formats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:124
msgid ""
"PDF, ePub and zipped HTML files are optional, and each one points to a "
"single file. They are shown in the :term:`flyout menu` like any other :doc:"
"`downloadable format </offline-formats>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:129
msgid ""
"- uses: readthedocs/upload-action@v1\n"
"  with:\n"
"    token: ${{ secrets.READTHEDOCS_TOKEN }}\n"
"    project-slug: <your-project-slug>\n"
"    html: _build/html\n"
"    pdf: _build/latex/documentation.pdf\n"
"    epub: _build/epub/documentation.epub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/build/direct-upload.rst:139
msgid ""
"$ readthedocs upload \\\n"
"    --project-slug <your-project-slug> \\\n"
"    --html _build/html \\\n"
"    --pdf _build/latex/documentation.pdf \\\n"
"    --epub _build/epub/documentation.epub"
msgstr ""

